#: ../../../library-medium.rst:390
msgid ""
"``0.1 + 0.2`` is ``0.30000000000000004`` due to binary floating point, but "
"``math.isclose`` compares within a relative tolerance and reports ``True``. "
"Plain ``==`` would give ``False``."
msgstr ""
"``0.1 + 0.2`` es ``0.30000000000000004`` debido al punto flotante binario, "
"pero ``math.isclose`` compara dentro de una tolerancia relativa e informa "
"``True``. Un ``==`` simple daría ``False``."

#: ../../../library-medium.rst:412
msgid "``deque([2, 3, 4], maxlen=3)``"
msgstr "``deque([2, 3, 4], maxlen=3)``"

#: ../../../library-medium.rst:413
msgid "``deque([0, 1, 2], maxlen=3)``"
msgstr "``deque([0, 1, 2], maxlen=3)``"

#: ../../../library-medium.rst:414
msgid "``deque([0, 1, 2, 3, 4], maxlen=3)``"
msgstr "``deque([0, 1, 2, 3, 4], maxlen=3)``"

#: ../../../library-medium.rst:415
msgid "raises ``IndexError``"
msgstr "lanza ``IndexError``"

#: ../../../library-medium.rst:420
msgid ""
"A bounded ``deque`` silently drops items from the opposite end when it is "
"full. Appending on the right past ``maxlen=3`` evicts from the left, keeping"
" the last three values ``[2, 3, 4]``."
msgstr ""
"Un ``deque`` acotado descarta silenciosamente elementos del extremo opuesto "
"cuando está lleno. Añadir por la derecha superando ``maxlen=3`` expulsa por "
"la izquierda, conservando los tres últimos valores ``[2, 3, 4]``."

